a local test of relative inequalities</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>1953</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17719709</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.socscimed.2007.05.043</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Janssen</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyce</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name><name><surname>Simpson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Pickett</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of individual- and area-level measures of socioeconomic status on obesity, unhealthy eating, and physical inactivity in Canadian adolescents</article-title><source>Am J Clin Nutr</source><year>2006</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16400062</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gunnel</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kammerling</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Brooks</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Relation between parasuicide, suicide, psychiatric admissions, and socioeconomic deprivation</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1995</year><volume>311</volume><fpage>226</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7627035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kennedy</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Iveson</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Violence, homicide and suicide: strong c